When Enola talks about teaching a dog to sit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:58.320
the movie cuts to an advert for Dr&nbsp;
Pavlov's Patented Pooch Persuader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:03.600
Approved by Socks the Wonder Dog. 
This is an amusing reference to physiologist Ivan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.700
Pavlov's discovery that he could condition dogs&nbsp;
to salivate at the sound of a bell, by ringing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.500
bell whenever they were shown a plate of food.
After a while, the dogs associated the bell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:17.220
sound with food and salivated even&nbsp;
if they weren't brought any food.
&nbsp;

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:22.260
These principles of classical conditioning&nbsp;
are popularly known as Pavlov's dog.
&nbsp;

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:25.320
[barking]
By the way, if you pause here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.820
